# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/life.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event life_staircase
# en: The Staircase Moves
title [1e1113] = 楼梯动了
# en: Halfway up the west staircase, it decides to be somewhere else. You're now heading toward a floor you've never seen, at speed, and you're late for Arcana.
text [b49591] = 西楼梯爬到一半，它决定去别的地方。你正被高速送往一层你从没见过的楼，而你的奥术课要迟到了。
# en: A grand spiral staircase in mid-rotation, a student clinging to the banister as the steps swing toward a different floor.
scene [684196] = 一道宏伟的螺旋楼梯正在旋转，一个学生紧抓扶手，台阶正转向另一层楼。
# en: Hold on and see where it goes
opt.left.label [441219] = 抓紧，看它去哪儿
# en: It deposits you in a dusty forgotten classroom. In a desk: eight old crowns and a love letter from 1802.
opt.left.say.1 [0aecae] = 它把你放在一间落满灰尘、被遗忘的教室里。课桌里有八枚旧克朗和一封 1802 年的情书。
# en: It takes you to the roof. Then the cellar. Then the roof again. You miss Arcana entirely.
opt.left.say.2 [30a40f] = 它把你送上屋顶。然后是地窖。然后又是屋顶。你完美错过了整节奥术课。
# en: Jump for the landing
opt.right.label [fc3ab6] = 跳向平台
# en: You leap and land neatly. A passing portrait applauds.
opt.right.say.1 [e697a6] = 你一跃而起，稳稳落地。路过的一幅肖像画鼓起了掌。
# en: You leap and land, but not neatly. A passing portrait winces.
opt.right.say.2 [ff31a3] = 你一跃而起，落地了，但不太稳。路过的一幅肖像画皱了皱眉。

@event life_mystery_stew
# en: Mystery Stew
title [afd265] = 神秘炖菜
# en: Tonight's dinner is described on the board only as "Stew". It is grey-green. The ladle is standing up by itself. The cook is watching you with hope.
text [70292b] = 今晚的晚餐在菜单板上只写着“炖菜”。它是灰绿色的。汤勺自己立在里面。厨师满怀希望地看着你。
# en: A huge cauldron of grey-green stew in the dining hall, a ladle standing upright in it unaided.
scene [1a7e62] = 餐厅里一大锅灰绿色的炖菜，一把汤勺自己笔直地立在锅中。
# en: Eat it bravely
opt.left.label [b372d7] = 勇敢地吃下去
# en: It's... delicious? Rich, peppery, faintly glowing. You go back for seconds. The cook beams.
opt.left.say.1 [768d2a] = 它……很好吃？浓郁、带着胡椒味，还微微发光。你又去盛了一碗。厨师笑开了花。
# en: It's not delicious. It's not anything a stomach should know about. You spend the night regretting it.
opt.left.say.2 [995531] = 不好吃。它不是任何胃应该认识的东西。你后悔了一整晚。
# en: Toast and jam again
opt.right.label [31a8e9] = 还是吐司配果酱
# en: You eat toast. The cook looks hurt. You feel guilty all evening.
opt.right.say.1 [e74e29] = 你吃了吐司。厨师一脸受伤。你内疚了一整晚。

@event life_lost_wand
# en: Where Is Your Wand?
title [e9e5f4] = 你的魔杖呢？
# en: Your wand is gone. It was on your desk. Now it isn't. Classes start in twenty minutes.
text [006487] = 你的魔杖不见了。它刚才还在桌上。现在没了。二十分钟后就要上课了。
# en: A dormitory turned upside down, clothes everywhere, a student on hands and knees peering under a bed.
scene [9d31f7] = 一间被翻得底朝天的宿舍，衣服扔得到处都是，一个学生趴在地上往床底下看。
# en: Tear the room apart
opt.left.label [a2a2bf] = 把房间翻个底朝天
# en: It's in your boot. Why is it in your boot? You make it to class with seconds to spare.
opt.left.say.1 [f6b100] = 它在你的靴子里。它为什么会在你靴子里？你在最后几秒赶到了教室。
# en: You find it at lunch, inside the pillowcase. You've missed a whole morning.
opt.left.say.2 [2b5185] = 午饭时你在枕套里找到了它。你错过了整整一上午。
# en: Try a summoning charm
opt.right.label [18e9e7] = 试试召唤咒
# en: It flies into your hand from inside the wardrobe, offended at having been lost.
opt.right.say.1 [d8a6af] = 它从衣柜里飞进你手里，对自己被弄丢一事颇为不满。
# en: Every pencil in the dormitory flies at your face. The wand stays hidden out of spite.
opt.right.say.2 [1fe091] = 宿舍里每一支铅笔都朝你脸上飞来。魔杖出于怨气，继续藏着。

@event life_snoring_roommate
# en: The Snorer
title [b3c66f] = 打呼噜的人
# en: Someone in your dormitory snores like a dragon with a head cold, and nobody will admit to it. You haven't slept properly in a week.
text [ab60f0] = 宿舍里有人打起呼噜来像一条感冒的龙，而且没人承认。你已经一个星期没睡好了。
# en: A dark dormitory, one bed shaking with snores so loud the curtains flutter, another occupant glaring with a pillow over their head.
scene [a2130d] = 漆黑的宿舍里，一张床随着震天的呼噜声摇晃，窗帘都在飘，另一个人用枕头捂着头怒目而视。
# en: Brew a silencing draught
opt.left.label [716d57] = 熬一剂静音药剂
# en: Perfect silence. Too perfect. The culprit, the quiet one by the window, is now silent even when awake. It wears off by Tuesday.
opt.left.say.1 [ab759f] = 完美的寂静。太完美了。罪魁祸首——靠窗那个安静的家伙——现在醒着也发不出声音。到周二才失效。
# en: The draught finds the wrong bed. Now two people snore, in harmony.
opt.left.say.2 [80815d] = 药剂找错了床。现在有两个人在打呼噜，还是和声。
# en: Move to the common room sofa
opt.right.label [65d659] = 搬到公共休息室的沙发上
# en: You sleep on the sofa and meet everyone who comes down at 3am. Some of them are very interesting.
opt.right.say.1 [168a41] = 你睡在沙发上，结识了每一个凌晨三点下楼的人。其中有些人非常有意思。

@event life_portrait_gossip
# en: The Portraits Talk
title [b767ea] = 肖像画在说话
# en: Two portraits in the east gallery are gossiping about a student. Then one of them says your name and they both go suspiciously quiet.
text [feda64] = 东画廊里两幅肖像画正在八卦某个学生。然后其中一幅说出了你的名字，两幅画都可疑地安静了下来。
# en: A long gallery of gilded portraits, painted figures leaning out of their frames toward each other, whispering behind painted hands.
scene [58f7f0] = 长长的画廊里挂满镀金肖像，画中人探出画框凑在一起，用画出来的手捂着嘴窃窃私语。
# en: Bribe them with flattery
opt.left.label [729d7c] = 用奉承贿赂它们
# en: Ten minutes of compliments on their brushwork, and they tell you everything. Gossip about half the faculty, too.
opt.left.say.1 [b45427] = 夸了十分钟它们的笔触，它们就什么都告诉你了。还附送了半个教职员团队的八卦。
# en: "Flattery," sniffs the duchess, "is so common." They turn their backs. Literally.
opt.left.say.2 [20a283] = “奉承，”公爵夫人嗤之以鼻，“太俗气了。”它们背过身去。字面意义上的。
# en: Pretend you didn't hear
opt.right.label [e071a6] = 假装没听见
# en: You walk on. Behind you, the whispering resumes, louder.
opt.right.say.1 [546c2f] = 你继续往前走。身后，窃窃私语又响了起来，更大声了。

@event life_pixies
# en: Pixie Infestation
title [12ac66] = 小精灵泛滥
# en: Someone left a window open and the dormitory is now full of pixies. They're stealing socks, unscrewing bedposts and laughing in very high voices.
text [53332f] = 有人没关窗户，宿舍里现在满是小精灵。它们在偷袜子、拧床柱，还用尖细的嗓音大笑。
# en: A dormitory full of tiny blue winged creatures swinging from curtains, stealing socks and pulling hair.
scene [9a096c] = 宿舍里到处是蓝色带翅膀的小生物，荡在窗帘上，偷袜子，扯头发。
# en: Fight them off
opt.left.label [a5f0b8] = 把它们打跑
# en: You catch nine with a laundry bag. The dorm cheers. The pixies swear at you, colourfully.
opt.left.say.1 [db8849] = 你用洗衣袋抓住了九只。宿舍一片欢呼。小精灵们花样百出地骂你。
# en: You lose. The pixies hang you from the chandelier by your robe. It takes an hour to get down.
opt.left.say.2 [87d5ba] = 你输了。小精灵把你的长袍挂在吊灯上，连人一起。你花了一个小时才下来。
# en: Bribe them with sugar
opt.right.label [8661f5] = 用糖贿赂它们
# en: You lay a trail of sugar cubes out of the window. The pixies follow it, munching, and leave one sock as a tip.
opt.right.say.1 [ace496] = 你在窗外铺了一路方糖。小精灵们边吃边跟着走了，还留下一只袜子当小费。

@event life_gargoyle
# en: A Talkative Gargoyle
title [7093dd] = 话痨石像鬼
# en: The gargoyle above the east door clears its throat as you pass. "You," it rumbles. "You look like someone who'd listen. Nobody listens to gargoyles."
text [4162d1] = 你经过时，东门上方的石像鬼清了清嗓子。“你，”它低沉地说，“你看起来像会听人说话的人。没人愿意听石像鬼说话。”
# en: A weathered stone gargoyle on a parapet, one eye open, mouth moving, a student sitting beside it with a sandwich.
scene [2eb36a] = 护墙上一尊饱经风霜的石像鬼睁着一只眼，嘴在动，一个学生拿着三明治坐在它旁边。
# en: Hurry along
opt.left.label [1a6798] = 赶紧走开
# en: "Typical," says the gargoyle. It sulks until spring.
opt.left.say.1 [852a4c] = “典型。”石像鬼说。它一直闷闷不乐到了春天。
# en: Sit and listen
opt.right.label [1a3cf5] = 坐下来听
# en: It tells you three hundred years of academy gossip, including where the founders hid the good biscuits. You find the biscuits.
opt.right.say.1 [3415ec] = 它给你讲了三百年的学院八卦，包括创始者把好饼干藏在了哪里。你找到了那些饼干。

@event life_brownies
# en: Help in the Night
title [fae0e4] = 夜里的帮手
# en: You wake to find your desk tidied, your socks darned and your essay proofread. Brownies. They expect something in return. Traditionally: cream.
text [bfda31] = 你醒来发现书桌被收拾整齐、袜子被补好、论文被校对过了。是棕仙。它们期待回报。按照传统：奶油。
# en: Tiny bearded figures in aprons tidying a cluttered student desk by moonlight, one darning a sock.
scene [bb94a0] = 月光下，系着围裙的长胡子小人在整理一张凌乱的书桌，其中一个在补袜子。
# en: Leave out a bowl of cream
opt.left.label [a73198] = 放一碗奶油
# en: Your room stays spotless all term. Your essays have suspiciously good spelling.
opt.left.say.1 [f0b341] = 整个学期你的房间都一尘不染。你的论文拼写好得可疑。
# en: Leave them nothing
opt.right.label [760b5f] = 什么都不留
# en: The next morning, every one of your socks is tied in knots. Brownies keep score.
opt.right.say.1 [ac042b] = 第二天早上，你的每一只袜子都被打了结。棕仙是记账的。

@event life_midnight_snack
# en: Midnight Hunger
title [5673a0] = 午夜饥饿
# en: It's midnight and you're starving. The kitchens are three floors down, past a prefect's post.
text [d97eb5] = 午夜了，你饿得要命。厨房在三层楼下，要经过一个级长的岗哨。
# en: A student in pyjamas tiptoeing past a sleeping prefect toward a door marked KITCHENS, a candle cupped in their hand.
scene [6a7e01] = 一个穿睡衣的学生踮着脚经过打盹的级长，走向一扇写着“厨房”的门，双手护着一支蜡烛。
# en: Go back to bed hungry
opt.left.label [6a67a5] = 饿着回去睡
# en: You dream of sandwiches. Long, detailed, beautiful sandwiches.
opt.left.say.1 [d77265] = 你梦见了三明治。长长的、细节丰富的、美丽的三明治。
# en: Sneak down
opt.right.label [a9ae15] = 偷偷溜下去
# en: Cold pie, a pot of custard, a heel of bread. Feast of kings.
opt.right.say.1 [2a2136] = 冷馅饼、一罐蛋奶冻、一块面包头。帝王盛宴。
# en: The prefect is awake. You spend a week washing the pots you were trying to raid.
opt.right.say.2 [151ad8] = 级长醒着。你洗了一星期你本想去偷吃的那些锅。

@event life_insomnia
# en: The Ceiling at 3am
title [bbad03] = 凌晨三点的天花板
# en: You can't sleep. Your brain has decided to replay every embarrassing thing you've said since you were six.
text [0cce8a] = 你睡不着。你的大脑决定把你六岁以来说过的每一句丢人的话都重播一遍。
# en: A student lying awake staring at a ceiling where faint painted stars have started slowly moving.
scene [eda828] = 一个学生睁眼躺着，盯着天花板，上面画着的淡淡星星开始缓缓移动。
# en: Get up and study
opt.left.label [dd9384] = 起床学习
# en: By dawn you've read three chapters and remembered one of them.
opt.left.say.1 [d35323] = 到天亮时你读了三章，记住了其中一章。
# en: Brew chamomile and count the painted stars
opt.right.label [d3506b] = 泡杯洋甘菊茶，数天花板上的星星
# en: Halfway through counting, the stars start counting back. Then you're asleep.
opt.right.say.1 [297bdf] = 数到一半，星星开始反过来数你。然后你就睡着了。

@event life_morning_run
# en: The Dawn Run
title [97a783] = 黎明晨跑
# en: A group of students runs the lakeshore every dawn. They've invited you. It's very early. It's very cold.
text [b909a7] = 有一群学生每天黎明沿着湖岸跑步。他们邀请了你。很早。很冷。
# en: The lakeshore path at dawn, mist on the water, a lone runner's breath steaming, the towers catching the first gold light.
scene [0d10ee] = 黎明的湖岸小路，水面上浮着薄雾，一个孤独的跑者呼着白气，塔楼映着第一缕金光。
# en: Sleep in
opt.left.label [de2af7] = 睡懒觉
# en: You hear them come back, glowing and smug. You are warm and unrepentant.
opt.left.say.1 [58ff7c] = 你听见他们回来了，容光焕发，一脸得意。你暖暖和和，毫无悔意。
# en: Run with them
opt.right.label [8e7ee8] = 和他们一起跑
# en: You nearly die at the first mile and feel immortal by the third. The lake shines like a coin. You feel every step of it all through your lectures.
opt.right.say.1 [2e95a0] = 第一英里你差点死掉，到第三英里你觉得自己长生不老。湖面亮得像一枚硬币。整堂课上，你都能感觉到每一步的后劲。

@event life_homework_mountain
# en: The Pile
title [654764] = 作业山
# en: Three essays, a potion log, a star chart and a reading list the length of your arm. All due this week. The pile has achieved its own weather.
text [68b440] = 三篇论文、一份药剂日志、一张星图，还有一份和你胳膊一样长的阅读书单。全部本周截止。这座作业山已经形成了自己的小气候。
# en: A desk buried under a precarious tower of scrolls and books, a student peeking hopelessly over the top.
scene [7c65a4] = 书桌被一座摇摇欲坠的卷轴和书本之塔淹没，一个学生绝望地从塔顶探出头来。
# en: Grind through it
opt.left.label [6c90f1] = 埋头苦干
# en: You finish at 4am on the last day. Every piece is handed in. You sleep through breakfast.
opt.left.say.1 [2f2b04] = 最后一天凌晨四点你全部完成。每一份都交上去了。你睡过了早饭。
# en: Pick what matters, skip the rest
opt.right.label [321412] = 挑重要的做，其余的跳过
# en: You hand in two of five and go for a walk. The professors are not pleased. You feel great, temporarily.
opt.right.say.1 [c142df] = 你交了五份中的两份，然后出去散步了。教授们不太高兴。你感觉好极了，暂时。

@event life_stolen_answers
# en: The Answers
title [48b36f] = 答案
# en: A third-year is selling copies of next week's exam. Eight crowns. "Guaranteed real," he whispers. "Straight from the examiner's desk."
text [3aac85] = 一个三年级生在卖下周考试的复印件。八克朗。“保真，”他低声说，“直接从考官桌上拿的。”
# en: A folded paper being passed under a library table, the faint glow of an examiner's seal on it.
scene [fab1a5] = 一张折好的纸从图书馆桌下传过，上面隐隐闪着考官的印章。
# en: Walk away
opt.left.label [96da1a] = 走开
# en: Two weeks later, five students who bought copies are suspended. The answers were fake.
opt.left.say.1 [882a6f] = 两周后，买了复印件的五个学生被停学了。那些答案是假的。
# en: Buy a copy
opt.right.label [cae18d] = 买一份
# en: They're real. You ace it. You also can't quite look the examiner in the eye.
opt.right.say.1 [80fd8d] = 是真的。你考得很好。你也没法直视考官的眼睛了。
# en: They're fake, and planted. You're caught with a copy. Detention, and a very cold letter home.
opt.right.say.2 [aaad15] = 是假的，而且是个圈套。你被抓到持有复印件。禁闭，外加一封非常冰冷的家书。

@event life_backfire
# en: Spell Backfire
title [195f68] = 咒语反噬
# en: You mispronounce a minor cheering charm in the corridor. Something goes wrong. Every time you hiccup, a tiny firework comes out.
text [4df613] = 你在走廊里把一个小小的振奋咒念错了。出了点问题。现在你每打一个嗝，就会冒出一朵小烟花。
# en: A student mid-hiccup, a small firework bursting from their mouth, classmates ducking.
scene [89a5a5] = 一个学生正在打嗝，一朵小烟花从嘴里炸开，同学们纷纷闪躲。
# en: Go to the infirmary
opt.left.label [f09b9c] = 去医务室
# en: Sister Amaranth cures it in a minute and charges you three crowns. "For the ceiling," she says.
opt.left.say.1 [4e5350] = 阿玛兰斯修女一分钟就治好了，收了你三克朗。“赔天花板的。”她说。
# en: Live with it
opt.right.label [a97cce] = 就这么过吧
# en: You become briefly famous as "the sparkler". It's not the fame you wanted.
opt.right.say.1 [01b18e] = 你作为“烟花人”短暂地出了名。这不是你想要的那种出名。

@event life_lake_swim
# en: A Swim in the Lake
title [939267] = 湖中游泳
# en: It's hot and the whole year has gone down to the jetty. Something large is rumoured to live in the deep part. People are swimming anyway.
text [9f8141] = 天很热，整个年级都跑到栈桥边去了。传说湖的深处住着什么大东西。大家还是照游不误。
# en: Students leaping off a wooden jetty into a sparkling lake on a hot afternoon, something large and dark moving far beneath the surface.
scene [36073b] = 炎热的午后，学生们从木栈桥跳进波光粼粼的湖里，水面下极深处有个巨大的黑影在移动。
# en: Stay on the jetty
opt.left.label [a30932] = 待在栈桥上
# en: You dangle your feet and eat cherries. Something brushes your toe. You keep your feet up after that.
opt.left.say.1 [5776ea] = 你晃着脚丫吃樱桃。有什么东西擦过你的脚趾。从那以后你一直把脚抬着。
# en: Dive in
opt.right.label [eb830e] = 跳下去
# en: In the deep part, you open your eyes underwater and see a round door, far below, glowing. Then you need air.
opt.right.say.1 [0ca583] = 在深水区，你在水下睁开眼，看见很深很深的地方有一扇圆门在发光。然后你需要换气了。
# en: The water's perfect. Something large and friendly swims under you, and you decide not to panic.
opt.right.say.2 [0e8868] = 水温完美。有个友善的大家伙从你身下游过，你决定不慌。

@event life_stray_cat
# en: A Cat Moves In
title [9441a9] = 猫搬进来了
# en: A black cat with one torn ear is sitting on your pillow. It looks at you as though you are the one trespassing.
text [f24184] = 一只耳朵缺了一角的黑猫正坐在你的枕头上。它看着你，好像闯进来的人是你。
# en: A scruffy black cat sitting on a dormitory pillow as if it has always lived there, one torn ear, very green eyes.
scene [2adf64] = 一只邋遢的黑猫坐在宿舍枕头上，仿佛一直住在这里，一只耳朵破了，眼睛绿得发亮。
# en: Shoo it out
opt.left.label [bd0ff5] = 把它赶出去
# en: It leaves with enormous dignity and moves in with your neighbour, who spoils it rotten.
opt.left.say.1 [73a8df] = 它极其庄重地离开了，搬去和你的邻居住，邻居把它宠上了天。
# en: Let it stay
opt.right.label [b09a3c] = 让它留下
# en: It's called Professor now. It sleeps on your homework. You've never been happier.
opt.right.say.1 [7e205d] = 它现在叫“教授”。它睡在你的作业上。你从没这么幸福过。

@event life_storm_night
# en: The Lights Go Out
title [3af5ad] = 灯灭了
# en: A storm knocks out every light-crystal in the dormitory. The common room fills with students, blankets and somebody's terrible ghost story.
text [cb21f0] = 一场风暴让宿舍里所有的光晶石都熄灭了。公共休息室里挤满了学生、毯子，和某人讲的烂透了的鬼故事。
# en: A dark common room lit only by lightning, students huddled under blankets, one telling a ghost story.
scene [09a304] = 漆黑的公共休息室只被闪电照亮，学生们裹着毯子挤在一起，有人在讲鬼故事。
# en: Tell an even scarier story
opt.left.label [36f701] = 讲个更吓人的故事
# en: Your story is so good that three people sleep with the lights on for a week. You're a legend.
opt.left.say.1 [d941b3] = 你的故事太好了，有三个人开着灯睡了一个星期。你成了传奇。
# en: Your story is not scary. It is, however, accidentally hilarious.
opt.left.say.2 [226bee] = 你的故事不吓人。不过，意外地非常好笑。
# en: Light the room with a spell
opt.right.label [928a24] = 用咒语照亮房间
# en: You fill the room with soft floating lights. Someone starts singing. It turns into the best night of term.
opt.right.say.1 [a9ec71] = 你让屋里飘满柔和的光点。有人唱起了歌。那成了本学期最美好的一夜。
# en: You light the sofa. Briefly. The storm seems less frightening after that.
opt.right.say.2 [725129] = 你点着了沙发。短暂地。那之后，风暴似乎也没那么可怕了。

@event life_mirror_talks
# en: The Honest Mirror
title [11488a] = 诚实的镜子
# en: The bathroom mirror has started commenting on your appearance. "Hair," it says this morning. Just: "Hair."
text [197720] = 浴室的镜子开始点评你的外表了。今天早上它说：“头发。”就两个字：“头发。”
# en: A bathroom mirror with a stern painted face in its silvering, frowning at a student mid-toothbrush.
scene [bed5d4] = 一面浴室镜子的镀银里嵌着一张严肃的画中脸，正对着刷牙刷到一半的学生皱眉。
# en: Ask for its advice
opt.left.label [97bf15] = 向它请教
# en: It turns out to be an excellent stylist. You look great. You hate that it's right.
opt.left.say.1 [88d699] = 原来它是个出色的造型师。你看起来棒极了。你讨厌它说得对。
# en: Cover it with a towel
opt.right.label [719e1f] = 用毛巾盖住它
# en: It sulks under the towel. Muffled: "Hair."
opt.right.say.1 [2b3d43] = 它在毛巾下面生闷气。闷声闷气地：“头发。”

@event life_prank_war
# en: Prank War
title [562813] = 恶作剧大战
# en: The dormitory across the corridor turned your door into a goat. The goat is fine. Honour, however, demands retaliation.
text [a19079] = 走廊对面的宿舍把你的门变成了一只山羊。山羊没事。然而荣誉要求你报复。
# en: A corridor ankle-deep in enchanted soap bubbles, two dormitories' worth of students hurling them at each other.
scene [9791ed] = 走廊里没过脚踝的魔法肥皂泡，两个宿舍的学生互相扔着泡泡。
# en: Rise above it
opt.left.label [fe2376] = 不跟他们计较
# en: You take the high road. The goat eats your homework. You let it.
opt.left.say.1 [f7115b] = 你选择了高尚。山羊吃了你的作业。你随它去了。
# en: Retaliate
opt.right.label [5cb1e8] = 报复回去
# en: You fill their dorm with a thousand singing bubbles. They concede by dawn.
opt.right.say.1 [59c97e] = 你让他们宿舍里塞满了一千个会唱歌的泡泡。天亮前他们就认输了。
# en: You're caught carrying a crate of bubbles. Detention, but the goat seems proud of you.
opt.right.say.2 [aee56b] = 你抱着一箱泡泡时被逮住了。禁闭，但那只山羊似乎为你骄傲。
# en: Glamour their door into a goat
opt.up.label [9c44fe] = 用魅影把他们的门变成山羊
# en: You return the compliment with a glamour: their door becomes a goat, an extremely convincing one, which bleats when knocked. It lasts three days. Nobody can prove a thing.
opt.up.say.1 [d28289] = 你用一道魅影回敬：他们的门变成了一只山羊，逼真极了，一敲门就咩咩叫。这持续了三天。谁也拿不出证据。

@event life_mail_owl
# en: The Wrong Letter
title [38e547] = 送错的信
# en: A delivery owl drops a scented pink letter in your porridge. It's addressed to someone else. It's a love letter. It's very, very passionate.
text [6296cf] = 一只送信猫头鹰把一封带香味的粉色信扔进了你的粥里。收件人不是你。是封情书。非常、非常热烈的情书。
# en: A ruffled delivery owl dropping a scented pink envelope onto a breakfast plate, a student looking up in confusion.
scene [2c78c3] = 一只羽毛凌乱的送信猫头鹰把一只带香味的粉色信封扔到早餐盘上，一个学生困惑地抬起头。
# en: Deliver it to its owner
opt.left.label [6dedfd] = 把它送给收信人
# en: The recipient goes crimson and thanks you. Two weeks later, they're holding hands with the sender in the dining hall.
opt.left.say.1 [364f07] = 收信人满脸通红地向你道谢。两周后，他们和写信人在餐厅里手牵着手。
# en: Read it first
opt.right.label [e728e4] = 先读一读
# en: You read it. You will never be able to look the potions professor in the eye again.
opt.right.say.1 [038e70] = 你读了。你再也无法直视魔药教授的眼睛了。

@event life_money_from_home
# en: A Parcel From Home
title [0fa1f2] = 家里寄来的包裹
# en: A parcel from home: a knitted scarf, a jar of jam, a note telling you to eat vegetables, and a small purse of coins.
text [e2ed27] = 一个家里寄来的包裹：一条织好的围巾、一罐果酱、一张叮嘱你多吃蔬菜的字条，还有一小袋硬币。
# en: A brown paper parcel tied with string on a dormitory bed, a knitted scarf, a jar of jam and a small coin purse spilling out.
scene [632059] = 宿舍床上一个用绳子捆着的牛皮纸包裹，露出一条针织围巾、一罐果酱和一只小钱袋。
# en: Save the money
opt.left.label [59078b] = 把钱存起来
# en: You tuck it away. The jam lasts six days.
opt.left.say.1 [c9f65f] = 你把钱收好。果酱吃了六天。
# en: Spend it on a treat for your friends
opt.right.label [c9ff29] = 请朋友们吃点好的
# en: Cake from the village for everyone. You're popular for an entire afternoon.
opt.right.say.1 [182e55] = 从镇上买了蛋糕分给大家。你受欢迎了整整一个下午。

@event life_found_purse
# en: A Purse in the Grass
title [558b87] = 草丛里的钱袋
# en: A fat velvet purse lies in the grass by the path. Thirty crowns at least. Embroidered initials: A.T.
text [bc1f08] = 小路边的草丛里躺着一只鼓鼓的天鹅绒钱袋。至少三十克朗。上面绣着缩写：A.T.
# en: A velvet purse lying in the long grass beside a path, coins glinting at its open mouth, initials embroidered on it.
scene [b64283] = 小路旁长草间躺着一只天鹅绒钱袋，袋口露出闪亮的硬币，上面绣着姓名缩写。
# en: Return it to its owner
opt.left.label [c3ae44] = 物归原主
# en: A.T. turns out to be Aldric Thorne. He takes the purse and stares at you a long moment. "Honest," he says. It sounds like a diagnosis.
opt.left.say.1 [ccc630] = A.T. 原来是奥尔德里克·索恩。他接过钱袋，盯着你看了很久。“诚实。”他说。听起来像是诊断结果。
# en: Keep it
opt.right.label [87c2f5] = 据为己有
# en: Thirty crowns richer. A few days later, Thorne mentions in class that he lost something. He looks at no one in particular.
opt.right.say.1 [3a88fb] = 你多了三十克朗。几天后，索恩在课上提到他丢了东西。他没有特意看向任何人。

@event life_peddler
# en: The Travelling Peddler
title [c295f6] = 行脚商人
# en: A peddler's wagon has parked by the gates. "Lucky charms! Genuine article! Thirty crowns, and fortune follows you for a season!"
text [985dd5] = 一辆货郎车停在了校门边。“幸运护身符！货真价实！三十克朗，好运伴你一整季！”
# en: A gaudy painted wagon at the academy gates, hung with lanterns and trinkets, a peddler with a gold tooth grinning.
scene [aca905] = 学院门口一辆花哨的彩绘货车，挂满灯笼和小玩意儿，一个镶金牙的货郎咧嘴笑着。
# en: Buy a lucky charm
opt.left.label [00deab] = 买个幸运护身符
# en: 30 gold
opt.left.hint [54caf0] = 30 金币
# en: It's a real one. Things go right all month. You start talking to it.
opt.left.say.1 [eb2634] = 是真货。整个月诸事顺遂。你开始跟它说话了。
# en: It turns your neck green. Fortune does not follow you. The peddler is long gone.
opt.left.say.2 [a11a74] = 它把你的脖子染绿了。好运并没有跟着你。货郎早就跑没影了。
# en: Just browse
opt.right.label [dbbc5f] = 随便看看
# en: You buy nothing and enjoy a sugared apple and the peddler's outrageous stories.
opt.right.say.1 [017402] = 你什么都没买，享受了一只糖苹果和货郎天花乱坠的故事。

@event life_bookshop
# en: Sale at Grimsby's
title [89ece4] = 格林斯比书店大促
# en: Grimsby's Books is having a sale. An old copy of "Advanced Arcane Theory" for fifteen crowns. Normally forty. It's annotated, apparently, by a famous wizard.
text [e4e3d1] = 格林斯比书店在打折。一本旧版《高等奥术理论》只要十五克朗。平时要四十。据说上面有一位著名巫师的批注。
# en: A crooked bookshop with books stacked to the ceiling, a hand-painted sign in the window reading HALF OFF, MOSTLY.
scene [3daef9] = 一家歪歪扭扭的书店，书一直堆到天花板，橱窗上手绘的招牌写着：半价，大部分。
# en: Buy it
opt.left.label [0aa234] = 买下
# en: 15 gold
opt.left.hint [05537f] = 15 金币
# en: The annotations are brilliant, rude and occasionally about the author's divorce. You learn a great deal.
opt.left.say.1 [0f1da3] = 批注精彩、刻薄，偶尔还聊到作者的离婚。你学到了很多。
# en: Leave it
opt.right.label [3e2fed] = 算了
# en: You walk away. You think about it for weeks.
opt.right.say.1 [08ccd0] = 你走开了。接下来好几周你都在惦记它。

@event life_new_robes
# en: Shabby Robes
title [a4fae7] = 破旧的长袍
# en: Your robes are fraying at every hem. Someone at dinner called them "vintage". It was not a compliment.
text [afc5fd] = 你的长袍每一处下摆都磨毛了。晚饭时有人说它们很“复古”。那可不是夸奖。
# en: A student in a hall mirror holding up a fraying sleeve, a tailor's flyer in their other hand.
scene [c82b72] = 一个学生站在大厅的镜子前，举起磨毛的袖子，另一只手里拿着裁缝铺的传单。
# en: Patch them yourself
opt.left.label [475422] = 自己缝补
# en: Your stitching is crooked but cheerful. Some people start copying it.
opt.left.say.1 [019c7e] = 你的针脚歪歪扭扭，却很欢快。有些人开始模仿了。
# en: Buy new robes (30 gold)
opt.right.label [ed7264] = 买新长袍（30 金币）
# en: 30 gold
opt.right.hint [54caf0] = 30 金币
# en: Midnight-blue wool, silver trim. People actually turn to look. You walk differently all week.
opt.right.say.1 [2c96cc] = 午夜蓝的羊毛，银色镶边。人们真的会回头看。你一整周走路的姿势都不一样了。

@event life_card_game
# en: A Game of Wizard's Hand
title [7c9c91] = 一局巫师牌
# en: A late-night game of Wizard's Hand. The cards change faces when no one's looking. The pot is thirty crowns. The upper-years look hungry.
text [0d1104] = 深夜的一局巫师牌。没人看时，牌面会自己变。奖池三十克朗。高年级生们看起来很饿。
# en: A smoky corner of the common room, students around a low table with cards and coins, one card floating and changing face.
scene [404f4d] = 公共休息室烟雾缭绕的角落，学生们围着矮桌打牌，桌上堆着硬币，一张牌浮在空中变换牌面。
# en: Play
opt.left.label [ab6f83] = 下场
# en: You read every bluff and keep a straight face. Thirty crowns and a reputation.
opt.left.say.1 [36d8bf] = 你识破了每一次虚张声势，始终面不改色。三十克朗，外加名声。
# en: You lose fifteen crowns and the upper-years' respect, in that order.
opt.left.say.2 [47f34e] = 你输掉了十五克朗和高年级生的尊重，按这个顺序。
# en: Watch and learn
opt.right.label [37e8ef] = 看着学
# en: You learn more watching than you would have playing. Mostly about who cheats.
opt.right.say.1 [11df36] = 你看到的比下场玩学到的还多。主要是谁在出老千。

@event life_essay_prize
# en: The Essay Prize
title [f26093] = 论文奖
# en: The Lumen Essay Prize: thirty crowns for the best essay on "Magic and Duty". The deadline is Friday. You have an idea already.
text [04145b] = 流明论文奖：五十克朗，奖给以“魔法与责任”为题的最佳论文。周五截止。你已经有了一个想法。
# en: A brass plaque on a noticeboard announcing THE LUMEN ESSAY PRIZE — 50 CROWNS, a quill pinned beneath it.
scene [a84625] = 布告栏上一块黄铜牌宣布“流明论文奖——50 克朗”，下面钉着一支羽毛笔。
# en: Enter
opt.left.label [f863ad] = 参赛
# en: You win. Your essay is read aloud at dinner. You don't know where to look.
opt.left.say.1 [1ea809] = 你赢了。晚饭时你的论文被当众朗读。你不知道眼睛该往哪儿看。
# en: You don't win, but the judges' notes are glowing. Next year, maybe.
opt.left.say.2 [f33231] = 你没赢，但评委的点评赞不绝口。也许明年吧。
# en: Skip it
opt.right.label [9909cb] = 不参加
# en: The winner reads their essay aloud at dinner. Yours would have been better. Probably.
opt.right.say.1 [f95dff] = 晚饭时获奖者朗读了自己的论文。你的本来会更好。大概吧。

@event life_charity
# en: The Winter Fund
title [04edf0] = 冬季基金
# en: The village winter fund is collecting for families who can't afford fuel this winter. The jar is half full.
text [cf1ae3] = 小镇冬季基金正在为今冬买不起柴火的家庭募捐。募捐罐已经满了一半。
# en: A collection jar shaped like a lantern on the dining hall table, half full of coins, a hand-lettered sign: FOR THE VILLAGE WINTER FUND.
scene [cb02b0] = 餐厅桌上一只灯笼形状的募捐罐，半满的硬币，手写的牌子：小镇冬季基金。
# en: Donate fifteen crowns
opt.left.label [645481] = 捐十五克朗
# en: 15 gold
opt.left.hint [05537f] = 15 金币
# en: Your name goes on a little list by the jar. You feel warm, which is the point.
opt.left.say.1 [e202cc] = 你的名字被写进了罐子旁边的小名单。你觉得心里暖暖的，这正是意义所在。
# en: Walk past
opt.right.label [d5359c] = 走过去
# en: You walk past. The jar fills anyway. You think about it on cold nights.
opt.right.say.1 [2eee4f] = 你走了过去。罐子还是被装满了。寒冷的夜里，你会想起这件事。

@event life_shady_offer
# en: A Quiet Job
title [c6d337] = 一份安静的差事
# en: A hooded figure behind the tavern: "Deliver this envelope to the boathouse at midnight. Don't open it. Thirty crowns." The envelope is warm.
text [0048f1] = 酒馆后巷里一个戴兜帽的人：“午夜把这封信送到船屋。别拆开。三十克朗。”信封是温的。
# en: A hooded figure in an alley behind the village tavern holding out a sealed envelope, a purse visible in their other hand.
scene [7d377f] = 镇上酒馆后的小巷里，一个戴兜帽的身影递出一封封好的信，另一只手里露出钱袋。
# en: Refuse
opt.left.label [cada35] = 拒绝
# en: The figure melts into the dark. The next morning, someone's boat is missing.
opt.left.say.1 [9eb4b8] = 那人融进了黑暗。第二天早上，有人的船不见了。
# en: Do the job
opt.right.label [573204] = 接下这份差事
# en: You make the drop. Bram is watching from the boathouse window. He writes something down.
opt.right.say.1 [e54d21] = 你送到了。布拉姆正从船屋的窗口看着。他记下了什么。
# en: You make the drop. Nobody sees. Thirty crowns, and a slightly cold feeling in your stomach.
opt.right.say.2 [43913a] = 你送到了。没人看见。三十克朗，外加胃里一点凉飕飕的感觉。

@event life_food_poisoning
# en: The Fish Was Off
title [e4f066] = 鱼坏了
# en: The fish pie at dinner was a mistake. Your stomach is staging a revolution.
text [cd4a4a] = 晚饭的鱼肉馅饼是个错误。你的胃正在闹革命。
# en: A student curled on a dormitory bed clutching their stomach, a half-eaten fish pie on the bedside table.
scene [4844ba] = 一个学生蜷缩在宿舍床上捂着肚子，床头柜上放着吃了一半的鱼肉馅饼。
# en: Ride it out
opt.left.label [43478c] = 硬扛过去
# en: A miserable night. You never look at fish pie again.
opt.left.say.1 [6ff02f] = 悲惨的一夜。你再也不看鱼肉馅饼一眼了。
# en: Get a tonic from the infirmary
opt.right.label [16a4f3] = 去医务室拿药
# en: The tonic tastes like old pennies, but it works.
opt.right.say.1 [f9e7fb] = 药尝起来像旧铜板，但是管用。

@event life_self_doubt
# en: Imposter
title [ee3a4e] = 冒牌货
# en: Everyone around you seems to belong here more than you do. They cast faster, learn quicker, laugh easier. Maybe the letter was a mistake.
text [5f044e] = 你身边的每个人似乎都比你更属于这里。他们施法更快、学得更快、笑得更自在。也许那封录取信是个错误。
# en: A student sitting alone on the edge of a fountain at night, staring at their reflection broken up by ripples.
scene [1842d0] = 夜里一个学生独自坐在喷泉边沿，盯着被涟漪打碎的倒影。
# en: Write down everything you've learned
opt.left.label [19e441] = 写下你学到的一切
# en: The list is longer than you expected. Much longer. You pin it above your bed.
opt.left.say.1 [c065df] = 清单比你想象的长。长得多。你把它钉在了床头。
# en: Talk to someone about it
opt.right.label [9fbd4a] = 找人聊聊
# en: Your friend laughs — not at you. "You? Everyone thinks you're the one who belongs." It helps more than you can say.
opt.right.say.1 [eac20a] = 你的朋友笑了——不是在笑你。“你？大家都觉得你才是那个真正属于这里的人。”这比你能说出口的还要管用。
# en: You talk to the night porter. He tells you everyone feels this way. You decide to believe him.
opt.right.say.2 [bebf73] = 你和守夜门房聊了聊。他告诉你每个人都有这种感觉。你决定相信他。

@event life_sleepwalking
# en: Sleepwalking
title [8fc4f7] = 梦游
# en: You wake up on the battlements in your pyjamas, at the very edge, with no memory of how you got there. Your feet are wet with lake water.
text [8d1ce1] = 你醒来时穿着睡衣站在城垛上，就在最边缘，完全不记得自己是怎么上来的。你的脚被湖水打湿了。
# en: A student in pyjamas standing on a moonlit battlement, eyes closed, one foot raised over the edge, an owl watching.
scene [ee10e3] = 月光下一个穿睡衣的学生站在城垛上，双眼紧闭，一只脚悬在边缘外，一只猫头鹰在旁观。
# en: Tell Sister Amaranth
opt.left.label [3f4d80] = 告诉阿玛兰斯修女
# en: A sleeping draught and a stern warning. It doesn't happen again.
opt.left.say.1 [c0917f] = 一剂安眠药和一番严厉的警告。再也没发生过。
# en: Keep it to yourself
opt.right.label [09de43] = 自己藏着
# en: It happens twice more. Each time you're facing the lake. Each time, you're a little closer to the water.
opt.right.say.1 [bd1bd8] = 又发生了两次。每一次你都面朝湖水。每一次，你都离水更近一点。
# en: It doesn't happen again. You start locking your door from the inside, just in case.
opt.right.say.2 [3c9aa9] = 再也没发生过。你开始从里面反锁房门，以防万一。

@event life_quiet_afternoon
# en: A Quiet Afternoon
title [4b76f8] = 安静的午后
# en: For once, nothing is due, nobody needs you, and the sun is out. A whole afternoon, unclaimed.
text [135c6b] = 难得一次，没有作业要交，没有人需要你，太阳也出来了。一整个午后，无人认领。
# en: A student lying in the long grass under an oak tree, a book open on their chest, clouds drifting above the towers.
scene [9574c3] = 一个学生躺在橡树下的长草里，一本书摊在胸口，云朵飘过塔楼上空。
# en: Nap under the oak tree
opt.left.label [320d04] = 在橡树下打个盹
# en: You wake to find a bird sitting on your book. It seems content. So are you.
opt.left.say.1 [6fb673] = 你醒来时发现一只鸟落在你的书上。它看起来很满足。你也是。
# en: Practise spells in the meadow
opt.right.label [2c28fa] = 在草地上练习咒语
# en: You make dandelion seeds dance in spirals for an hour. Nobody sees. It's perfect.
opt.right.say.1 [2cbd71] = 你让蒲公英的种子跳了一个小时的螺旋舞。没人看见。完美。

@event life_injury_stairs
# en: The Trick Step
title [cc11b3] = 陷阱台阶
# en: The ninth step on the north stair is a trick step. Everyone knows. You forgot. Your leg sinks to the knee and the stair holds on.
text [9cc7ba] = 北楼梯的第九级是陷阱台阶。人人都知道。你忘了。你的腿陷到了膝盖，台阶紧紧咬住不放。
# en: A stone staircase with one step glowing faintly, a student mid-fall, books flying everywhere.
scene [02874d] = 一道石阶上有一级微微发光，一个学生正往下摔，书本飞得到处都是。
# en: Wait for someone to help
opt.left.label [8e8e6b] = 等人来帮忙
# en: Forty minutes later, a first-year pulls you out. You're late for everything.
opt.left.say.1 [be4901] = 四十分钟后，一个一年级生把你拔了出来。你什么都迟到了。
# en: Wrench yourself free
opt.right.label [ec2221] = 硬把腿拔出来
# en: You pull free with a pop. Your shoe stays in the stair forever.
opt.right.say.1 [652719] = 你“啵”的一声挣脱了。你的鞋永远留在了台阶里。
# en: Something in your knee goes click. Not a good click.
opt.right.say.2 [17703b] = 你膝盖里有什么东西咔哒响了一声。不是好的那种咔哒。

@event life_lake_fever
# en: Lake Fever Season
title [5e2ca1] = 湖热病季节
# en: Half your dormitory has Lake Fever. Noses are glowing blue. You feel a tickle in your throat.
text [77a4bc] = 你宿舍里一半的人得了湖热病。鼻子都泛着蓝光。你觉得喉咙有点痒。
# en: A dormitory where half the beds hold sniffling students with faintly blue-glowing noses, tissues everywhere.
scene [87b40c] = 宿舍里半数床位躺着吸鼻子的学生，鼻头泛着淡淡的蓝光，纸巾扔得到处都是。
# en: Dose up on Maud's tea
opt.left.label [f3b875] = 猛灌莫德的茶
# en: Maud's lemon-and-thunder tea keeps you upright through the whole outbreak.
opt.left.say.1 [b6b4d0] = 莫德那杯柠檬加雷声的茶让你挺过了整场流行病。
# en: The tea from the kitchens isn't the same. Your nose starts glowing on Thursday.
opt.left.say.2 [9b0859] = 厨房的茶不是一回事。周四你的鼻子开始发光了。
# en: You dodge it. Somehow.
opt.left.say.3 [61efce] = 你躲过去了。不知怎么做到的。
# en: Keep going as normal
opt.right.label [5303bd] = 照常生活
# en: You keep going as normal for exactly two days.
opt.right.say.1 [68c5c6] = 你照常生活了整整两天。
# en: Iron constitution. You sail through. Everyone hates you a little.
opt.right.say.2 [7e0fc1] = 铁打的体质。你安然度过。大家都有点恨你。

@event life_first_snow
# en: First Snow
title [16a8b8] = 初雪
# en: The first snow of winter falls overnight and the whole academy wakes up giddy. Classes are optional, officially. Unofficially, they're cancelled by snowball.
text [59861c] = 冬天的第一场雪在夜里落下，整个学院醒来时都兴奋不已。官方说法是课程自愿参加。非官方说法是课程被雪球取消了。
# en: The academy courtyard blanketed in fresh snow, students mid-snowball fight, a snowman wearing a professor's hat.
scene [c59afe] = 学院庭院铺满新雪，学生们正在打雪仗，一个雪人戴着教授的帽子。
# en: Join the snowball war
opt.left.label [dd3116] = 加入雪仗
# en: You take a snowball to the face from the headmistress herself. Her aim is terrifying.
opt.left.say.1 [286cf4] = 你脸上挨了一个雪球——是院长本人扔的。她的准头吓死人。
# en: Your side wins. You build a snow-fort that lasts until Thawmoon.
opt.left.say.2 [d4a0aa] = 你们这边赢了。你堆的雪堡一直立到了融雪月。
# en: Hot chocolate by the fire
opt.right.label [cba09c] = 在炉边喝热可可
# en: You watch from the window, warm and smug, while the snowballs fly.
opt.right.say.1 [da3e9c] = 你在窗边看着雪球横飞，暖和又得意。

@event life_spring_cleaning
# en: Spring Cleaning
title [757d73] = 春季大扫除
# en: Spring cleaning. The brooms are enchanted, but the enchantment needs supervising. Your dorm's brooms have formed a union.
text [cd3829] = 春季大扫除。扫帚都施了魔法，但魔法需要监督。你们宿舍的扫帚成立了工会。
# en: A dormitory with every window thrown open, brooms sweeping by themselves, dust swirling in sunbeams.
scene [d4aefd] = 宿舍里所有窗户都敞开着，扫帚自己扫着地，灰尘在阳光里打转。
# en: Negotiate with the brooms
opt.left.label [086b0c] = 和扫帚谈判
# en: You agree to one day off a week and a polish. The dorm sparkles.
opt.left.say.1 [627f3a] = 你同意每周给它们放一天假，外加一次抛光。宿舍焕然一新。
# en: The brooms do not accept your terms. They sweep you into a cupboard.
opt.left.say.2 [56e3e0] = 扫帚们不接受你的条件。它们把你扫进了柜子里。
# en: Clean by hand
opt.right.label [7a78f4] = 亲手打扫
# en: An afternoon of scrubbing. It's oddly satisfying. You find three lost quills and a sandwich from Thawmoon.
opt.right.say.1 [ffa004] = 擦洗了一个下午。出奇地让人满足。你找到了三支丢失的羽毛笔和一个融雪月的三明治。

@event life_summer_heat
# en: The Heat
title [24ddd6] = 酷暑
# en: The heat is unbearable. Even the gargoyles are sweating. The lake is crowded, the library stifling, the dormitories ovens.
text [b86aba] = 热得让人受不了。连石像鬼都在冒汗。湖边挤满了人，图书馆闷得透不过气，宿舍就是烤炉。
# en: Students lying flat on the cool stone floor of a shaded colloquy, fanning themselves with exam papers.
scene [ecf9e7] = 学生们平躺在阴凉讲堂冰凉的石地板上，用考卷扇着风。
# en: Cast a cooling charm on your room
opt.left.label [71928c] = 给房间施个降温咒
# en: Your room becomes an icebox. People pay to visit. You let them for free. Mostly.
opt.left.say.1 [4b7a2e] = 你的房间变成了冰窖。有人付钱来参观。你让他们免费进来。大部分人。
# en: You make it colder. Briefly. Then hotter. Then it rains inside.
opt.left.say.2 [fdb685] = 你让它变冷了。短暂地。然后变得更热了。然后屋里下起了雨。
# en: Sleep on the roof
opt.right.label [3e5cc0] = 睡在屋顶上
# en: You sleep under the stars with half the dormitory. It's the best idea anyone's had all year.
opt.right.say.1 [d71668] = 你和半个宿舍的人一起睡在星空下。这是今年所有人想出来的最好的主意。

@event life_harvest_festival
# en: The Harvest Feast
title [d8f2a6] = 丰收宴
# en: The Harvest Feast: pies the size of cartwheels, cider, and a pumpkin carved to look like the headmistress, which she pretends not to notice.
text [e532a4] = 丰收宴：车轮那么大的馅饼，苹果酒，还有一个刻成院长模样的南瓜——她假装没注意到。
# en: Long tables groaning under pies and roast vegetables, candles floating above, a giant pumpkin carved like the headmistress.
scene [749624] = 长桌上堆满了馅饼和烤蔬菜，蜡烛浮在上方，一个巨大的南瓜被刻成了院长的模样。
# en: Eat until you can't move
opt.left.label [36bf14] = 吃到动不了为止
# en: You eat three helpings of everything. You're carried back to the dorm by friends. Worth it.
opt.left.say.1 [0f7497] = 每样东西你都吃了三份。朋友们把你抬回了宿舍。值了。
# en: Help in the kitchens for extra pay
opt.right.label [9e76c8] = 去厨房帮忙赚外快
# en: You serve pie to the entire academy. The cooks slip you coins and a whole pie of your own.
opt.right.say.1 [05b6e2] = 你给全院的人端馅饼。厨师们悄悄塞给你一些硬币，还有一整个属于你的馅饼。

@event life_rival_academy
# en: Visitors From Thornwick
title [ac57b9] = 荆木来客
# en: A delegation from Thornwick Academy is visiting. Their students are smug, polished and very loudly unimpressed with Lumenhold's plumbing.
text [6ee3f7] = 荆木学院的代表团来访。他们的学生傲慢、体面，而且非常大声地对流明堡的水管表示不屑。
# en: A delegation of students in green robes marching through the gates, noses raised, a Lumenhold crowd watching suspiciously.
scene [78c6a2] = 一队身穿绿袍的学生昂首阔步地走进校门，流明堡的人群怀疑地注视着他们。
# en: Be a gracious host
opt.left.label [071642] = 做个大方的东道主
# en: You show them the observatory. One of them admits, grudgingly, that it's better than theirs.
opt.left.say.1 [a32053] = 你带他们参观了天文台。其中一人不情不愿地承认，这比他们的好。
# en: Defend Lumenhold's honour
opt.right.label [cfa83c] = 捍卫流明堡的荣誉
# en: You challenge their best to a friendly duel and win. The Thornwick students are quieter at dinner.
opt.right.say.1 [291905] = 你向他们最强的人发起友谊决斗，并且赢了。晚饭时荆木的学生安静多了。
# en: You challenge their best to a friendly duel and lose, quite unfriendly. Thornwick will be insufferable.
opt.right.say.2 [ad3104] = 你向他们最强的人发起友谊决斗，然后输得一点也不友谊。荆木的人会嚣张得让人受不了了。

@event life_lost_firstyear
# en: A Lost First-Year
title [ed808e] = 迷路的一年级生
# en: A tiny first-year is standing in the middle of the corridor, clutching an upside-down timetable and trying very hard not to cry.
text [a1cbbc] = 一个小个子一年级生站在走廊中间，攥着一张拿倒了的课表，拼命忍着不哭。
# en: A tiny first-year in enormous robes standing in the middle of a junction of five identical corridors, clutching a timetable upside down.
scene [6a5ef7] = 一个穿着宽大长袍的小个子一年级生站在五条一模一样的走廊交汇处，倒拿着课表。
# en: Point the way and hurry on
opt.left.label [ee0d43] = 指个路就赶紧走
# en: You point. They go the wrong way anyway. You hope they're all right.
opt.left.say.1 [f7d5b2] = 你指了路。对方还是走错了。你希望对方没事。
# en: Walk them to class
opt.right.label [e53c7b] = 送对方去教室
# en: You walk them all the way and they talk the entire time. You're late, but they've decided you're their hero.
opt.right.say.1 [344963] = 你一路把对方送到，对方一路说个不停。你迟到了，但对方已经认定你是自己的英雄。

@event life_frog_escape
# en: The Frogs Are Out
title [abdd0d] = 青蛙跑出来了
# en: Someone knocked over the frog crate in Potions. Thirty frogs are loose. One has climbed into the professor's hat. He has not noticed yet.
text [0c896d] = 有人在魔药课上打翻了青蛙箱。三十只青蛙跑了出来。一只爬进了教授的帽子里。他还没发现。
# en: A potions classroom overrun by dozens of hopping green frogs, one sitting smugly on the professor's desk.
scene [8a2633] = 魔药教室里到处是蹦跳的绿青蛙，一只得意地蹲在教授的讲台上。
# en: Help round them up
opt.left.label [d47151] = 帮忙把它们抓回来
# en: You catch eleven, a personal best. The professor finds the hat frog at dinner. You were not involved.
opt.left.say.1 [87225e] = 你抓了十一只，个人最佳纪录。教授在晚饭时发现了帽子里的那只。与你无关。
# en: Quietly let a few escape out the window
opt.right.label [73e9bc] = 悄悄放几只从窗户逃走
# en: Five frogs hop to freedom in the lake. You feel like a liberator.
opt.right.say.1 [076f02] = 五只青蛙跳进湖里重获自由。你觉得自己像个解放者。

@event life_fortune_teller
# en: The Village Fortune-Teller
title [203728] = 镇上的算命婆
# en: In the village, an old fortune-teller beckons you into her tent. "Three crowns for your future, dearie. Eight for a good one."
text [b16d5c] = 在镇上，一个算命的老婆婆招手让你进她的帐篷。“三克朗算你的未来，孩子。八克朗算个好的。”
# en: A beaded doorway into a tiny dim tent, an old woman with a crystal ball and too many rings beckoning.
scene [0e06ff] = 一顶昏暗小帐篷的珠帘门口，一个戴着太多戒指、捧着水晶球的老妇人在招手。
# en: Pay three crowns
opt.left.label [557fdf] = 付三克朗
# en: "You will meet a tall stranger." You already have. Several. It's an academy.
opt.left.say.1 [74a51c] = “你会遇到一个高个子陌生人。”你已经遇到了。好几个。这是所学院。
# en: "Beware of water." She won't say more. You think about the lake a lot.
opt.left.say.2 [6db734] = “小心水。”她不肯再多说。你常常想起那片湖。
# en: Pay eight crowns
opt.right.label [196642] = 付八克朗
# en: Your future is wonderful. She's very specific. You are fairly sure she's making it up, and you don't care.
opt.right.say.1 [7d6032] = 你的未来美好极了。她说得非常具体。你很确定她是在瞎编，而你不在乎。

@event life_volunteer
# en: Clean-Up Duty
title [2e9a08] = 清理值日
# en: After the storm, the grounds are a wreck. Volunteers needed to help clear branches and rebuild the hen-house. No pay. Lots of mud.
text [540f81] = 风暴过后，校园一片狼藉。需要志愿者帮忙清理断枝、重建鸡舍。没有报酬。满地泥巴。
# en: Students in rolled-up sleeves raking leaves on the great lawn, a groundskeeper directing them with a pitchfork.
scene [5de831] = 卷起袖子的学生们在大草坪上耙落叶，一位园丁拿着草叉指挥。
# en: Volunteer
opt.left.label [39a371] = 报名志愿
# en: A long day of mud and laughter. An old woman in a straw hat brings everyone cocoa and remembers your name.
opt.left.say.1 [e39352] = 漫长的一天，满身泥巴和笑声。一位戴草帽的老妇人给每个人送来了热可可，还记住了你的名字。
# en: Stay in and study
opt.right.label [6d8b57] = 留在屋里学习
# en: You study through the shouting and hammering outside. The hen-house is very nice when it's done.
opt.right.say.1 [1e9737] = 你在外面的喧闹和敲打声中学习。鸡舍建好后很漂亮。
